"Goodnight, Maya," Asha says.
"Goodnight, Asha."
"Thanks a lot," I say.
Asha goes to her home.
I close the door.
Now I am alone in the flat.
It is completely quiet in the house.
I sit on the sofa.
This sofa is very comfortable.
I look everywhere in the room.
All things are now in their places.
My laptop is kept on the table.
My books are near the laptop.
My clothes are in the cupboard.
The empty bag is under the bed.
The tea cups are in the kitchen.
My new flat is small and beautiful.
I feel very good.
Now I feel completely at home in Mumbai.
